{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785296511,"nonce":"SQAuzGIgqGWE+VzyzQt/YbQ5ZbI=","message":"RCA:\n\nCode path: src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:1141-1182 (_on_trailer callback in action_trailer), src/b4/review/_review.py:2617 (_parse_reply_trailers), _review.py:2657 (_remove_trailer_from_reply), src/b4/review_tui/_modals.py:125 (TrailerScreen.TRAILER_NAMES).\n\nWhen review['reply'] exists, _on_trailer treats the buffer as authoritative and syncs it to the menu selection:\n\n- current = _parse_reply_trailers(reply_text) collects ALL trailers in the buffer. find_trailers(followup=True) recognizes non-person trailers too — verified: 'Fixes: 1234567890ab (\"some patch\")' is returned as a trailer.\n- The removal loop (_review_app.py:1159-1163) removes every entry of current whose name is not in desired_lower, where desired comes from the TrailerScreen result.\n- TrailerScreen only offers ['Acked-by', 'Reviewed-by', 'Tested-by', 'NACKed-by'] (_modals.py:125), and pre-toggling maps existing trailers onto those four names only (_modals.py:127-135). A 'Fixes:' trailer in the buffer cannot be represented in the menu, so it is never part of result, and confirming the dialog with any selection removes it from the buffer via _remove_trailer_from_reply.\n- _remove_trailer_from_reply drops only the trailer line itself, keeping the blank separator lines on both sides — reproduced: the buffer is left with a doubled blank-line gap, matching the reporter's 'leaving 2 empty lines around'.\n\nThe same mechanism affects any hand-typed trailer the menu does not manage (Fixes:, Cc:, Suggested-by:, Link:, ...).\n\nRelated: the CRLF half of the same report is tracked separately (editor CRLF stored verbatim in reply buffer).","files":null}]}